cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SHOBS-P in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "SHOBS-P: Shiloh Hill Observatory Photometry"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "John W."
    family-names: "Armbrust"
    affiliation: "Shiloh Hill Observatory"
  - name: "Shiloh Hill Observatory"
version: "2.2.18"
date-released: "2026-10-18"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23417064"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/SHOBS-S/SHOBS-P"
abstract: >-
  A desktop application for differential aperture photometry with one-shot-color
  and monochrome astronomical cameras. Variables mode builds multi-night light
  curves with scintillation-aware error bars, period searches and AAVSO Extended
  reports; Transits mode fits exoplanet transits (Mandel and Agol model, MCMC)
  with a detected / inconclusive / none verdict and writes AAVSO exoplanet
  reports and ExoFOP packages; Discovery mode scans a whole field for variable
  stars.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - photometry
  - differential photometry
  - variable stars
  - exoplanets
  - transit photometry
  - AAVSO
  - citizen science
